{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/941902-regina-s-covenant-imbalance","id":941902,"title":"Regina's Covenant imbalance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T06:34:26-07:00","id":941902,"title":"Regina's Covenant imbalance","content":"How are you addressing the fact that Weihan Cynn and Gallows Post have significantly less powers written down than Lancea et Sanctum and Invictus (though they have no abilities in this book)? do you restrict Invictus/Sanctum players to merits only? allow Cynn/Gallows to use CotC and Carthian powers respectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:40:06-07:00","id":941933,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Not all covenants have powers. <br /> <br /> Though if you wanted to reason it out some members of the Weihan Cynn could have access to proto-Cruac. I'm sure someone else has figured some magic powers for the Gallow's Post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:50:13-07:00","id":942172,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the Gallows Post, but the possibilities for Contract with the Uncanny are endless, especially with a faction like &quot;mages&quot;. Who needs Cruac when you have indirect access to gifts, contracts and plain, supernal magic? With the right demon buddy, they can arrange a resurrection and how many vampires can honestly say that?<br /> <br /> This tends to leave me wondering what vampires can offer to other splats, besides being middlemen in this case. A lot of them are good controlling and killing people, but then other splats have ways around those. I suppose that their age makes them better sources for forgotten knowledge than some, but <i>accurate</i> chronicling isn't their fort\u00e9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:05:04-07:00","id":942560,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't count the Gallows Post under-powered either.<br /> <br /> While the Invictus has monopolized the upkeep of the Traditions and the Sanctified monopolize Christian affairs, the Gallows Post is pretty much the ones who decides who goes where outside of the Princedom and has a stranglehold over trading between Fiefs. Having access to resources and allies in ANY city is ludicrous, especially considering that no other Covenant will again have that kind of reach since the Post becomes a Broken Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:32:03-07:00","id":942633,"title":"","content":"Or, rather, all the covenants develop that kind of reach because modern transportation and globilization should not be underestimated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:23:21-07:00","id":942830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/941902-regina-s-covenant-imbalance?p=942633#post942633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, rather, all the covenants develop that kind of reach because modern transportation and globilization should not be underestimated?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Potato, potato (this sounded better in my head).<br /> <br /> If everybody has that kind of reach, nobody has the monopoly on it so it is not quite the same. I understand what you are trying to say though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:40:16-07:00","id":943651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in my game the Gallow's Post basically uses the criminal underground to hold power. Having a Gallow's Post member in the game will help going around a city easily, while if you don't accept their help, they will go out of their way to difficult things for you. Like any criminal group who holds a city.<br /> <br /> And the Cynn... those contracts are really useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}